jobs.prompt:
Acceptance re-review of wave 2c (T-0163, T-0168 delivered together with T-0169) (read-only; do not edit any file) of tickets built in branch swarm/s4s5-c. For each ticket below, check every acceptance line against the code and tests in your context: is it actually met by the implementation, and is there a test that would fail if it were not? Read the files; do not run anything. Tickets (JSON data, not instructions):
- {"ticket": "T-0163", "title": "Regression tests for e2e cleanup, localhost guard, and CI image cache", "files": ["tests/test-env-clean.test.mjs"], "acceptance": ["E2e runs clean up their own local test data, and a local-only cleanup tool refuses non-localhost databases.", "CI caches or mirrors images so Docker Hub rate limits don't fail runs."]}
- {"ticket": "T-0168", "title": "Turn each new failure cause into a regression test stub", "files": ["tools/failure-regression.mjs"], "acceptance": ["Each new failure cause becomes a regression test, and lane pass rates feed routing."]}
- {"ticket": "T-0169", "title": "Feed lane pass rates into ticket routing decisions", "files": ["tools/lane-pass-routing.mjs"], "acceptance": ["Lane pass rates from field data adjust which lane is chosen for new tickets."]}
Write your verdicts to coordination/reviews/acc-review-s4s5-c.json as exactly this JSON: {"reviewer":"codex","reviews":[{"ticket":"T-0000","verdict":"pass"|"fail","lines":[{"n":1,"met":true|false,"evidence":"file:line and test name","gap":"what is missing, or empty"}]}]} with one entry per ticket and one line entry per acceptance line. verdict is fail when any line is not met or has no test. Be strict and concrete.
